From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Max Schaefer <max@excloo.com>
Date: Sat, 07 Nov 2026 15:48:54 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Wake the haptic worker at its continuous-on limit

Refine the DRV2624 request worker introduced in patch 0914. An isolated
2000 ms request previously slept until its requested end before checking
the 1500 ms continuous-on limit. Extended requests could defer that check
as well.

Wake at the earlier of the requested end and the continuous-on deadline.
Keep the existing RTP level, request extension, stop and equal rest period
behaviour. Short pulses retain their original deadline.

---
diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_haptic.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_haptic.c
index a1ba3c7..8a82a65 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_haptic.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_haptic.c
@@ -560,16 +560,22 @@ hap_thread(void *arg __unused, wait_result_t wr __unused)
 		bool on = false;
 		uint8_t level = 0;
 		uint64_t until = 0, on_since = 0, rest_until = 0;
+		uint64_t max_on;
+		nanoseconds_to_absolutetime((uint64_t)HAP_MAX_ON_MS * NSEC_PER_MSEC, &max_on);
 		unsigned drives = 0;
 		while (hp.ready && !hp.dead) {
 			uint64_t now = mach_absolute_time(), deadline;
 			if (on) {
-				deadline = until;
+				/* Long or extended requests must still wake at the continuous-on limit. */
+				deadline = on_since + max_on;
+				if (until < deadline) {
+					deadline = until;
+				}
 			} else {
 				clock_interval_to_deadline(60000, NSEC_PER_MSEC, &deadline);
 			}
 			(void)assert_wait_deadline(&hap_req_chan, THREAD_UNINT, deadline);
-			if (hap_req != 0 || (on && now >= until)) {
+			if (hap_req != 0 || (on && now >= deadline)) {
 				clear_wait(current_thread(), THREAD_AWAKENED);
 			} else {
 				thread_block(THREAD_CONTINUE_NULL);
@@ -605,8 +611,6 @@ hap_thread(void *arg __unused, wait_result_t wr __unused)
 					hp.dead = true;
 				}
 			}
-			uint64_t max_on;
-			nanoseconds_to_absolutetime((uint64_t)HAP_MAX_ON_MS * NSEC_PER_MSEC, &max_on);
 			if (on && (now >= until || hp.dead || now - on_since >= max_on)) {
 				lck_mtx_lock(&sweet_haptic_lock);
 				(void)drv_bits(DRV_GO, 0x01, 0x00);
